{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["They said further: <b>Amalek dwells in the land of the Negev</b> — to hint that there is no spirit to enter the land from there, for all of them are mighty: Amalek in the south, the Canaanite in the west and in the east, and the Amorite in the mountain. They reported their mission and discouraged the heart of the people with a hint, out of their fear of Moses and Aaron. Now they responded to everything that Moses had commanded them, except for what he said, 'whether few or many' — they gave him no answer on this point, and likewise they mentioned nothing good, for it was their intention to say afterward to the people, 'It is a land that devours its inhabitants,' by way of calumny — and behold its people are few and very strong. Now the people understood their intent, and then the whole congregation that was there began to murmur. And this is the meaning of 'Caleb silenced' (וַיַּהַס כָּלֵב), for he silenced them and said, 'Let us go up at once ... for we are well able to do it' (לָהּ), to say: it is true that the people are strong, but we are stronger than they and than their fortified cities. Therefore he said 'to it' (לָהּ). Then the scouts answered and elaborated their words and said, 'We are not able to go up against the people, for it is stronger than we,' meaning, even the people if they come out against us into the field we cannot go up against them to wage battle, much less conquer from them cities fortified very greatly — for the sense of 'to go up against the people' is like the sense of 'choose for yourselves a man and let him come down to me' (1 Samuel 17:8) — language of those doing battle in the battle line."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:57.877427213Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}